      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "DrawMeshInstanced definitely has some uses, but in my testing with instancing a lot of grass, just placing down a lot of grass objects with polybrush and then running a mesh combining script on them provides noticeably better performance at a **relatively** small amounts of grass objects of 10k (+1ms vs 0.3-0.5ms). I then use LOD groups and occlusion culling to cull them.\n\nAnd even with 10k instances of grass quads it is still not enough to fit much of an area.\n\nCulling is another thing that is really rough without DrawMeshInstancedIndirect, trying to do culling in Udon was 15 times slower than in C# code (20ms vs 300ms), which means that even if Udon was as fast as a normal C# script it would still not be viable.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
